Page type: List (docs/page-design.md section 4); it already was one (ScrollViewKCM, ListView of ItemDelegate, sections,
entry details on a kcm.push sub-page), so the structure stays. systemdBoot key, desktop files, scripts and the unit
D-Bus handling are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Toolbar action "Add New" -> "Add…" (menu: Application…, Login Script…, Logout Script…): always labelled, with the
  ellipsis because it opens something. Row kcm_autostart/AddNew.
- Per-entry CheckBox -> Switch (on/off in a list row, section 3); same call setEntryEnabled, same accessible text.
- Empty state: explanation no longer points at a button name, and the placeholder carries the action "Add
  Application…" (section 3). It is hidden until the model was filled once (modelReset), so it does not flash.
- Markers added on rows that only had weak anchors. Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_autostart.tsv (outer repo).
  Inventory --strict: 10 rows ok, 0 lost.

Speed: Autostart::load() ran AutostartModel::load() synchronously: mkpath, directory listing of ~/.config/autostart
and the script dirs, one KDesktopFile parse per entry, creation of a Unit (async D-Bus GetUnit/GetAll) per entry
(autostartmodel.cpp load). It now runs from QTimer::singleShot(0), so the page is shown first and the list fills on
modelReset. The Unit calls were already asynchronous. usingSystemdBoot() (a config read per row binding) left as is.
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001/005, HIG-057. Not built yet. Unconfirmed: QTimer::singleShot with a pointer to the public non-slot
member AutostartModel::load (Qt 6 functor overload, should compile).

